 [:option {:value "70470"} "Team All-Around, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "70477"} "Floor Exercise, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "70479"} "Vault, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "70481"} "Parallel Bars, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "70483"} "Horizontal Bar, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "70485"} "Rings, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "70487"} "Pommelled Horse, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "70500"} "Team All-Around, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "70505"} "Floor Exercise, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "70507"} "Vault, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "70509"} "Uneven Bars, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "70511"} "Balance Beam, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "70171"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "70196"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "70233"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "70277"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "70321"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "70373"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "70431"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "70547"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "70605"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "70663"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "70721"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "70794"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "70878"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "259982"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "313009"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "353658"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19009152"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2012252"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/332"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Individual All-Around, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "21 – 24 July 1980"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/588"} "Dvorets sporta, Tsentralny stadion imeni V. I. Lenina, Moskva"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/70489"} "62 from 16 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The format was the same as in 1976. The team all-around was contested first, with the top 36 finishers from that event advancing to the individual all-around final. However, to prevent individual nations from dominating with over-representation, no more than three gymnasts from any one country could advance to the individual final. The total score consisted of 50% of the team all-around score and the performances on all four apparatuses in the individual final. The defending champion was " [:a {:href "/athletes/28995"} "Nadia Comăneci"] ", but there were chinks in her armor by 1980, as she had not won the World Championships in either 1978 or 1979 due to injury. The favorite in early 1980 was likely Soviet Yelena Mukhina who was the 1978 World Champion, missing the 1979 meet due to a broken leg. Sadly, a few weeks before the Moskva Olympics, Mukhina fell while training on floor exercise, broke her neck, and was rendered quadriplegic permanently. She would eventually die in 2006."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The contest for gold was very close between Comăneci, Soviet " [:a {:href "/athletes/29180"} "Yelena Davydova"] ", and East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/28499"} "Maxi Gnauck"] ". It all came down to the last rotation, with Gnauck leading but her vault scored only 9.70 points. Davydova then scored 9.95 on beam, and was followed by Comăneci on the same apparatus. She made a small stepback on landing, and it looked unlikely she would get the 9.95 she needed to win gold. The head judge was Romanian Marian Simionescu who disagreed with the judges’ scores and tried to get them to change them, arguing for 28 minutes before her complaint was disallowed. Simionescu refused to punch the final score into the computer which was done by a Soviet official while Simionescu continued her tirade. The 9.85 score gave Davydova the gold medal with Gnauck and Comăneci sharing silver."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This and the team all-around were Davydova’s only gold medals in Moskva, but she added a silver on beam in her only Olympics. Comăneci would win gold medals in 1980 on floor and beam, and ended her Olympic career with nine medals and five gold medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "66"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/29180"} "Yelena Davydova"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "79.150"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "50"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/28995"} "Nadia Comăneci"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROU.png"}] "ROU"]] [:td {} "79.075"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "18"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/28499"} "Maxi Gnauck"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "79.075"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "70"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/29209"} "Nataliya Shaposhnikova"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://o